      {
       "start": 3.4,
       "end": 8.422,
       "text": "Why try negative gains? A verified example.",
       "sceneId": "a01-escape"
      },
      {
       "start": 8.422,
       "end": 16.111,
       "text": "Six nodes, maxDiff 2, cut 6: every legal move has gain ≤ 0.",
       "sceneId": "a01-escape"
      },
      {
       "start": 16.111,
       "end": 22.244,
       "text": "Hill climbing stops at 6; FM takes A −1, B −1: cut 8.",
       "sceneId": "a01-escape"
      },
      {
       "start": 22.244,
       "end": 27.711,
       "text": "Now E's strongest tie is across: +4, cut 4.",
       "sceneId": "a01-escape"
      },
      {
       "start": 27.711,
       "end": 32.044,
       "text": "Exhaustive search confirms 4 is the balanced optimum.",
       "sceneId": "a01-escape"
      },
      {
       "start": 32.444,
       "end": 37.022,
       "text": "The attachment had its own example, with a claim.",
       "sceneId": "a02-legacy"
      },
      {
       "start": 37.022,
       "end": 42.711,
       "text": "Computed from its own data: the initial cut is 18, not 9.",
       "sceneId": "a02-legacy"
      },
      {
       "start": 42.711,
       "end": 46.4,
       "text": "E's move is legal, with gain +10.",
       "sceneId": "a02-legacy"
      },
      {
       "start": 46.4,
       "end": 51.2,
       "text": "Pass 1's best and the true optimum are both 8, not 4.",
       "sceneId": "a02-legacy"
      },
      {
       "start": 51.2,
       "end": 55.556,
       "text": "So it stays a regression test, not a lesson.",
       "sceneId": "a02-legacy"
      },
      {
       "start": 55.956,
       "end": 61.422,
       "text": "In real netlists a net often joins three or more cells.",
       "sceneId": "a03-multipin"
      },
      {
       "start": 61.422,
       "end": 67.333,
       "text": "A net {A, B, C, D}, weight 3, with only D on the right.",
       "sceneId": "a03-multipin"
      },
      {
       "start": 67.333,
       "end": 72.356,
       "text": "Counting pins: moving D gains +3, moving A gains 0.",
       "sceneId": "a03-multipin"
      },
      {
       "start": 72.356,
       "end": 77.489,
       "text": "Split into a clique and counted by edges, A would wrongly get −1.",
       "sceneId": "a03-multipin"
      },
      {
       "start": 77.889,
       "end": 81.8,
       "text": "The 1982 paper's speed comes from buckets.",
       "sceneId": "a04-bucket"
      },
      {
       "start": 81.8,
       "end": 88.156,
       "text": "One list per gain, plus a pointer to the largest legal gain.",
       "sceneId": "a04-bucket"
      },
      {
       "start": 88.156,
       "end": 94.489,
       "text": "Each move updates only its neighbours: a pass costs time in proportion to the pins.",
       "sceneId": "a04-bucket"
      },
      {
       "start": 94.489,
       "end": 102.178,
       "text": "This course updates gains incrementally, but still scans to choose: not O(P).",
       "sceneId": "a04-bucket"
      },
      {
       "start": 102.578,
       "end": 106.711,
       "text": "The window counts nodes, not area.",
